This function is already minimal, so the speedup will be small at best. The rewrite reads `profile` once into a local `const` pointer and marks the null and out-of-range branches as unlikely, which lets the compiler lay out the common path straight through. The checks, their order and the return values are unchanged, so behavior is identical.

```cpp
FIT_UINT16 Field::GetNumComponents(void) const
{
    const Profile::MESG* const p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return 0;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].numComponents;
}
```